 4. 🎸 Rewind and cash in 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Gerard Way of My Chemical Romance performs "Welcome to the Black Parade" in 2006. Photo: Theo Wargo/WireImage

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 We'll forgive you for thinking it's 2006 when you glance at the Billboard 200 this week.

 My Chemical Romance is topping the charts for the first time with a special edition re-release of its 20-year-old album "The Black Parade," AP reports . 🎧 State of play: The rock opera album — which couldn't top Disney's "Hannah Montana" on the charts two decades ago, coming in at No. 2 — sold the equivalent of 78,000 album units in the U.S. last week, according to Luminate.

 It's benefiting from a creative release strategy that involved 20 physical variants and six bonus tracks. 💭 Nathan's thought bubble: I suspect we'll see more retro music being re-released — in the same way that old movies are also having a moment in the theater — as stressed-out people pine for better days from the past.

 
 
